          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "l'ambulance is built on ambulant \"moving about\" (EtymDB), from Latin ambulāre \"to walk\" (Lewis & Short): first a field hospital that moved with an army."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
